CPEDAL 1
NAME "Lovepedal Kalamazoo Reference Draft"

# Reconstructed from the user's verified Effects Layouts drawing and the
# WhiteKeyHole trace published by La Revolution Deux / later clone layouts.
# This models the engaged signal path only. D5 polarity protection and LED /
# true-bypass wiring are intentionally omitted from the audio path.
#
# The first 4558 section is a non-inverting soft clipper with two silicon
# diodes in series in each feedback direction. The second section implements
# the separate Tone (treble softening) and Glass (high-frequency boost)
# behaviour described by Lovepedal.
#
# Cx across the first op-amp is optional on the Effects Layouts drawing and is
# omitted here. It can be introduced later as a component-variation control.

V VRAW VRAW 0 9
R R_SUPPLY VRAW VCC 100
C C_SUPPLY VCC 0 100n
C C_SUPPLY_BULK VCC 0 47u
AUDIO GUITAR INPUT 0 0.20

# Half-supply reference.
R R_VREF_TOP VCC VREF 10k
R R_VREF_BOTTOM VREF 0 10k
C C_VREF VREF 0 47u

# Input coupling / bias shown in the trace.
R R_INPUT_PD INPUT 0 1M
C C_IN INPUT CLIP_PLUS 47n
R R_INPUT_BIAS CLIP_PLUS VREF 1M

# First half of JRC4558: soft-clipping overdrive.
OPAMP U1A CLIP_PLUS CLIP_MINUS CLIP_OUT VCC 0 JRC4558

# Frequency-dependent non-inverting gain. Increasing DRIVE raises the feedback
# resistance and therefore the overdrive gain.
R R_GAIN_MIN GAIN_LOW VREF 3k3
C C_GAIN CLIP_MINUS GAIN_LOW 100n
POT DRIVE CLIP_OUT CLIP_MINUS CLIP_MINUS 500k LOG 0.58

# Two 1N914/1N4148 junctions in series for each feedback polarity.
D D1 CLIP_MINUS D12 1N914
D D2 D12 CLIP_OUT 1N914
D D3 CLIP_OUT D34 1N914
D D4 D34 CLIP_MINUS 1N914

# Passive Tone stage. The traced 5k control acts as a variable series
# resistance shunting the fixed 2.74k path; the 150n capacitor creates the
# treble roll-off. Higher GUI TONE intentionally means more treble softening,
# matching Lovepedal's published control description.
R R_POST_CLIP CLIP_OUT TONE_IN 1k
R R_TONE_FIXED TONE_IN TONE_NODE 2k74
POT TONE TONE_IN TONE_NODE TONE_NODE 5k LIN 0.45
C C_TONE TONE_NODE VREF 150n

# Second 4558 section. GLASS increases high-frequency closed-loop gain without
# removing low-frequency content: at low frequencies C_GLASS is effectively
# open, while at high frequencies it establishes the inverting-leg impedance.
OPAMP U1B TONE_NODE GLASS_MINUS AMP_OUT VCC 0 JRC4558
R R_GLASS_FB AMP_OUT GLASS_FB 1k
POT GLASS GLASS_FB GLASS_MINUS GLASS_MINUS 5k LIN 0.45
C C_GLASS GLASS_MINUS GLASS_RC 220n
R R_GLASS_SHUNT GLASS_RC VREF 332

# Output coupling and level.
C C_OUT AMP_OUT LEVEL_TOP 10u
POT LEVEL 0 OUT LEVEL_TOP 100k LIN 0.55
R R_OUT_LOAD OUT 0 1M

OUTPUT OUT 0.5
